course: dictionary
lesson: 462
title: Words for war and peace
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An armistice is an agreement between enemies in a war to stop fighting. The word hides a clue: the fighting stops, usually while both sides talk about peace.
explain: «The First World War ended with an armistice at 11 o'clock on 11 November 1918.» Ask what word would fit here. Try your meaning instead of the hard word: "The First World War ended with an agreement to stop fighting at 11 o'clock." It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Read the rest of the sentence for more clues. «...many countries keep two minutes' silence at that time each year.» People keep silence to remember something important, so the armistice must be a very important ending.
explain: Put both sentences together. «Korea has been divided since 1945, and the Korean War of 1950 to 1953 ended only in an armistice, not a peace treaty.» The words "only" and "not a peace treaty" show that an armistice is not the same as a full peace agreement: the fighting stopped, but peace was not signed.
fact: An armistice is an agreement between enemies to stop fighting in a war.
fact: Enemies usually agree an armistice while they talk about peace.
fact: «The First World War ended with an armistice at 11 o'clock on 11 November 1918.»
fact: Armistice Day, now Remembrance Day or Veterans Day, is marked with two minutes' silence and poppies.
fact: «The Korean War of 1950 to 1953 ended only in an armistice, not a peace treaty.»
exercise: «The First World War ended with an armistice at 11 o'clock on 11 November 1918.» What is an armistice? | *An agreement between enemies to stop fighting | A large army with many soldiers | A type of poppy flower | A winter holiday with snow and presents
exercise: «The Korean War ended only in an armistice, not a peace treaty.» What does this tell you about an armistice? | The war lasted only one day | Nobody fought in the war at all | Both sides signed a full peace treaty the same day | *Fighting stopped, but no full peace was signed
exercise: Many countries keep two minutes' silence on Remembrance Day. Why do they do this? | To celebrate the start of a holiday | To practise being quiet in class | To wait for the school bell | *To remember people who died in war
test: What is the best meaning of armistice? | A pet name for a soldier | A loud noise made by guns | *An agreement between enemies to stop fighting | A kind of map used in history lessons
test: In «the Korean War ended only in an armistice», what does the word only suggest? | Everyone was happy at the end | There were no soldiers at all | The war was very short and quick | *Fighting stopped, but there was no full peace
exam: Jayden asks, «What does armistice mean?» Which answer is best? | A long holiday from school | A kind of gun | A famous king | *A deal between enemies to stop fighting, usually while they talk about peace
